/target/
**/*.rs.bk
*.pdb

# Local data and secrets
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
*.sqlite
.env
session.json
exports/

# Scratch notes, if any ever land here. The instruction document is AGENTS.md,
# which is tracked.
/docs/

# Agent and editor scratch
.claude/

# What tools/capture/record.js writes: a browser profile holding a live
# session while it runs, and a log that still carries real usernames after
# the secrets are redacted. Neither is ever committed.
/tools/capture/out/

# Output the tool itself produces, if it lands in the repo root.
#
# All six extensions `output.rs` can write, not four. `.json` was the one
# missing, and it is the one that matters: `snob lists -o out.json` from here
# leaves a file full of real names, and `tests/common/mod.rs` already skips
# `exports/` for exactly that reason. Root-anchored, so the tracked
# `bucket/snob.json` is untouched; the negations are for the four documents
# that live at the root and are meant to be tracked.
/*.xlsx
/*.csv
/*.jpg
/*.png
/*.json
/*.ndjson
/*.jsonl
/*.md
!/README.md
!/CHANGELOG.md
!/AGENTS.md
!/CLAUDE.md
